## The Scenario options object
## 2026-08-20 — recovered and committed by a later iteration

Same failure mode as the MFS entry above: an iteration did the whole refactor,
left it in the working tree, and died before flipping the checkbox or
committing. Three modified files were waiting (App.tsx, tax.ts, tax.test.ts).
This iteration re-verified from scratch and committed them unchanged. The
write-up is reconstructed from the diff.

### What it replaced

`sizeConversion(ceiling, ordinary, ss, ltcg, filingStatus, seniors,
maxConversion, muni)` — eight positional arguments, six of them bare numbers,
and the backlog item recording that inserting `seniors` into the middle of that
list had already silently rebound App.tsx's `MAX_CONVERSION` to it once.

Now there is one `Scenario` interface — ordinaryIncome, ssBenefit, ltcg,
muniInterest, filingStatus, seniors, beneficiaries — every field optional, and
`resolveScenario()` fills the defaults. The same mistake is now a type error,
and an unknown key is a type error too, so a typo cannot quietly land on a
default.

Two things about that resolver are deliberate and worth not "simplifying":

- It is written out field by field rather than `{ ...DEFAULTS, ...scenario }`.
  A spread lets an explicit `{ ltcg: undefined }` — which
  `{ ...base, ltcg: someMaybeNumber }` produces at a call site — overwrite the
  default with undefined. Field-by-field `??` cannot.
- The sweeping functions take the range as a SECOND object
  (`marginalRateCurve(scenario, { maxIncome, step })`), because maxIncome/step
  describe the chart axis, not the taxpayer. Same for
  `ltcgMarginalRateCurve(scenario, { maxLTCG, step })`. Both overwrite the
  field they sweep, which is documented on each.

### The merge that fell out of it

`totalTax` and `totalTaxWithLTCG` became one function. They were already the
same computation — `totalTax` was just the ltcg=0 case — and once both took a
Scenario the signatures were identical, so keeping two was keeping a trap.
`totalTaxWithLTCG` is gone entirely; no references remain anywhere in src/.

Two helpers were extracted while the call sites were being rewritten:
- `agiFor(scenario)` = ordinary + ltcg + taxableSS. It is the base for the
  senior-deduction phaseout AND (plus muni) for IRMAA MAGI, and it was being
  open-coded in five places. `irmaaMagi` is now one line.
- The ordinary-bracket loop inside the old `totalTaxWithLTCG` was a duplicate
  of `federalIncomeTax`; it now just calls it.

`taxableSocialSecurity` now reads `ltcg` off the scenario itself instead of
making each caller pre-add it into an `otherIncome` argument. Check this when
touching the ordinary-income chart: that chart wants gains excluded, so
App.tsx passes a scenario with no `ltcg` — which is correct, and NOT an
oversight to be "fixed" by threading plannedLtcg in.

